// A theorem about an array: after completion, no entry is undecided.
//
// This is the example the README builds towards, and a miniature of the one
// property that made verification worth doing in tecack — where a partial
// stroke map is completed and then indexed *without a bounds check*, so a
// surviving sentinel is not a wrong answer but a WebAssembly trap.
//
// Everything here is integer. That is not incidental: MoonBit's verifier has
// no model of `Double`, and a function carrying a contract may not contain
// floating-point operations at all. The split this package demonstrates — put
// the index arithmetic where the solver can see it, leave the arithmetic that
// decides *values* outside — is what makes the technique applicable to a
// numeric algorithm in the first place.
options(
  "proof-enabled": true,
)
